context:
Project: an offline Hindi/English dictation app. Rust daemon, cpal audio capture into a lock-free ring buffer, Silero VAD, streaming Zipformer ASR via sherpa-onnx (int8, CPU). Target: cheap Windows laptops (i3, 8 GB), ~200 ms from key release to pasted text.

src/audio.rs:
```rust
pub fn on_audio(frames: &[f32], buf: &mut RingBuffer) {
    for f in frames { buf.push(*f); }
}

pub fn next_chunk(buf: &mut RingBuffer, vad: &mut Vad) -> Option<Vec<f32>> {
    let chunk = buf.pop_n(2560)?; // 160 ms at 16 kHz
    if vad.is_speech(&chunk) { Some(chunk) } else { None }
}
```
